WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.460
So, you binged Season 2 of Stranger Things
and got your fill of Eggos, demodogs, and

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.460
Snow Balls.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.099
But now you're wondering what's next?

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:12.240
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm looking at what we can

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.560
expect from Season 3 of the hit Netflix show,
which means I've got a heap of predictions

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.060
and theories as well as questions I'd love
to see answered in the series.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:25.160
So, I'll be discussing, among other things,
Eleven, the AV Club gang, Hopper, Max and

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.170
Billy, Kali, plus, of course, the Shadow Monster.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.210
By the way, my Stranger Things giveaway is
also running on this video, so, for your chance

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.210
to win a Stranger Things Funko Pop, make sure
you're subscribed to my channel and leave

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.260
me a comment below about what you'd like to
see happen in Season 3.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.890
Obviously I'm discussing season 2 in detail
and referencing season 1 as well, so take

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.250
care if you're not caught up.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.429
Before I get into individual theories and
predictions for characters, let's take a quick

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:55.329
look at what that creepy cliffhanger of the
Shadow Monster over Hawkins School in the

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:57.210
Upside Down means going forward.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:02.230
Of course, it's an intriguingly menacing and
ominous image to end on, but what really struck

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:07.120
me about it was that it feels like the monster
is almost stalking Eleven and the AV Club

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.120
gang.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.800
I mean, it stands to reason; after all, our
heroic friends were responsible for nixing

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.070
the Mind Flayer's nefarious plan and driving
it and its beastly minions out of their town.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.240
That's got to have riled up the sinister creature!

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.600
So, in Season 3, I think we could see the
Shadow Monster making a beeline for the kids,

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.900
especially Eleven, who he witnessed actually
closing the gateway in Hawkins Labs.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.090
I also wonder what happened to the portal
in the school corridor which Eleven used to

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.170
return from the Upside Down this season.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.970
It's the same spot which the Demogorgon used
in the first season to move from the Upside

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:42.270
Down to our world and if that opening is still
accessible, then it's something the Mind Flayer

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.880
could use to access Hawkins.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.380
Either way, we're going to see plenty more
of the Shadow Monster as the Duffer Brothers

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.540
have confirmed it will be an over-arching
villain for the series as a whole.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.580
By the end of the second season, Eleven learned
to control and intensify her powers to the

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.680
extent that she was able to close an enormous
breach between the Hawkins Lab and the Upside

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.680
Down.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.160
And perhaps we'll see her powers get even
stronger as the series progresses and she

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.940
doubtless tracks down other Hawkins Lab survivors.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.360
Potentially, there's a bit more stability
on the horizon for El, at least for the moment,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.360
as she's got an official birth certificate
that gives her a real name: Jane Hopper; meaning

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.070
that Chief Hopper is now her official father
figure.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.640
Though she does go to the Snow Ball, Dr Owens
suggests that Hopper keep El out of the spotlight

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.820
for a year, which could fit in with the time
jump to 1985 that I think we'll see next season.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.120
After all, the Duffer Brothers have talked
about the necessity of time jumps, like the

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.330
one between seasons 1 and 2, as the show's
young actors are all growing up.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:42.780
And, of course, setting Season 3 in 1985 would
bring some great stuff for the show to mine

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.460
including Back to the Future, Fright Night,
and The Breakfast Club.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.980
And maybe, after an off-screen year away from
prying eyes, though with visits from her friends,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.680
we could even see El venture out in the world,
joining Mike and the gang at school.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.990
And perhaps, as Joyce and Hopper get closer,
we'll also see them all form a sort of makeshift

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:00.990
family.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.330
Then, of course, there's still a couple of
other unresolved issues for Eleven which I

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.850
expect we'll also see addressed next season:
One is with her sister Kali who she left in

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:13.760
Chicago and another is with her Papa, Dr Brenner,
who we just discovered appears to be still

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.760
alive.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.819
And I'll talk about those a little later in
this video.

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:21.350
Season 2 introduced us to two new characters,
Max and Billy.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.630
Max was a fun addition who set up a new love
triangle with Dustin and Lucas vying for her

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.630
attention.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.940
By the end though, she'd proven she could
be a capable member of the AV Club party and

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.920
I expect that we'll see her take on a much
more active role next season.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:39.290
And given the influence of Dungeons and Dragons
on the show, maybe we'll see Max, who's pretty

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.870
nifty on her skateboard, take on the role
of a Dungeons and Dragons rogue, using her

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.319
speed and stealth to the group's advantage.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:50.790
Max's step-brother Billy was, of course, a
huge jerk throughout the season, to the point

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.290
where it made me wonder why the character
was introduced as he's so objectionable.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.540
However, I suspect that the showrunners have
something more interesting in mind for him

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:04.180
next season, which could also involve an affair
with Mrs Wheeler, Nancy and Mike's mum.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.500
Another theory, though, is that Billy could
be co-opted, willingly or not, by the Mind

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.360
Flayer into working on behalf of the evil
entity.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.860
Billy obviously has a lot of issues; there's
his relationship with his bullying father,

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.489
his apparent racism towards Lucas, his hostility
towards Max, and he may still be annoyed at

00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:21.949
her for stabbing him with a syringe in the
finale.

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:25.849
All of these feelings could take him to a
dark place where he ends up encountering the

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:30.830
Shadow Monster leading him to make a pact;
or like Will, he could end up taken over by

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.960
the Mind Flayer and get used as a human spy.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.430
And if that were the case, then this time,
the Shadow Monster would be in control of

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:41.650
someone who is already a brutal bully, rather
than the good-natured Will.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:46.070
And Billy wasn't the only thing taken down
in the finale at the Byers house.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:50.169
When Eleven reunited with Mike and friends,
she took out a set of demodogs circling the

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:51.169
house.

00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:55.520
But in a hilarious moment, Dustin then insisted
that Steve stuff one of the dead demodogs

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:00.139
into the Byers' fridge because "[it's] a ground-breaking
scientific discovery".

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:04.880
I'm hoping we might see the AV party investigate
the dead creature as it could reveal something

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.879
more about how the Mind Flayer creates and
controls its hive-minded minions.

00:05:08.879 --> 00:05:13.120
And I wonder if we'll see Dustin reach out
to his teacher Mr Clarke for help opening

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.729
this new curiosity door.

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:19.639
I mean, Mr Clarke has proven rather helpful
in the past, for example, giving advice about

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:24.759
making a sensory deprivation tank, so maybe
he'd have some tips about examining the demodog!

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:30.089
Or maybe Steve and Dustin will continue their
new-found bromance into next season with a

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:31.089
demodog dissection.

00:05:31.089 --> 00:05:35.659
Then again, it appears that Dr Owens is still
in town, despite the closure of Hawkins Lab,

00:05:35.659 --> 00:05:39.400
and he could well be interested in Dustin's
find.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.729
Despite his part in the cover-up, Owens did
help Hopper get a birth certificate for Eleven,

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:46.389
and so ended the season on a positive note.

00:05:46.389 --> 00:05:51.540
But maybe Owens will turn out to be a duplicitous,
scheming official, similar to actor Paul Reiser's

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:56.379
character Carter Burke in the movie Aliens,
which was such a big influence on this season

00:05:56.379 --> 00:05:57.379
of Stranger Things.

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:01.610
Oh, and let's not forget that the monster
likes the cold, so although the demodog is

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.340
dead, a fridge may still not be the best place
to keep it!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.990
Speaking of Dustin, the fact his nose and
mouth were covered by goggles and a scarf

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.160
in the tunnels didn't stop the spray from
a huge flower-like creature getting in his

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.160
mouth.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.449
And Hopper also got sprayed and trapped by
the vines when he first entered the tunnels

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:19.490
earlier in the season.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:24.099
Oh, and remember that Mike got caught in the
vines as well before being rescued by his

00:06:24.099 --> 00:06:25.099
friends.

00:06:25.099 --> 00:06:29.590
So, potentially, any of those three characters
could have been infected by the Monster.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.069
They all seem to be healthy at the end of
the season, but we can't rule out there being

00:06:33.069 --> 00:06:37.059
some sort of incubation period for any infection
they might be carrying.

00:06:37.059 --> 00:06:40.789
As for Will, it'll be interesting to see if
he still has visions of the Upside Down in

00:06:40.789 --> 00:06:44.659
Season 3, though the Duffer Brothers told
Variety that they think they'll 'need to give

00:06:44.659 --> 00:06:49.259
Will a breather' next season given everything
he's been through now for two years running.

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:54.309
The appearance in Season 2 of Kali, aka Eight,
who's another young survivor of Dr Brenner's

00:06:54.309 --> 00:06:58.939
secret experiments, confirms exactly what
many of us were thinking after last season:

00:06:58.939 --> 00:07:01.119
That there are others like Eleven out there.

00:07:01.119 --> 00:07:05.719
Now, it just remains to be seen how many others
of those ten who went before Eleven have survived.

00:07:05.719 --> 00:07:10.069
I fully expect to see a few of those survivors
in Season 3 and beyond.

00:07:10.069 --> 00:07:15.569
Unlike El, Kali is based in Chicago, and she
also has different powers to her lost sister

00:07:15.569 --> 00:07:18.990
as she's able to make people see or not see
whatever she chooses.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:23.530
So, the question for similar survivors going
forward is what they're up to now, what their

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:27.249
particular powers will be, and how and where
they will appear.

00:07:27.249 --> 00:07:31.249
Given that Kali was found in Illinois, the
state next to Indiana, I wonder if other survivors

00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:35.309
will turn up in other surrounding states such
as Ohio, Kentucky or Michigan.

00:07:35.309 --> 00:07:38.379
Also, will any of them join Kali on her revenge
mission?

00:07:38.379 --> 00:07:42.279
Or, what I suspect will happen in perhaps
the final season, is we'll find them teaming

00:07:42.279 --> 00:07:46.469
up with Eleven to eventually overcome the
terrors of the Upside Down once and for all.

00:07:46.469 --> 00:07:50.039
I've got a separate video where I explain
all the hidden clues in the show about which

00:07:50.039 --> 00:07:52.139
new gifted children we'll see next season.

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:56.460
You can tap in the top right to watch that
or there are links to it in the video description

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.129
and at the end of this video.

00:07:58.129 --> 00:08:03.499
Before this season, El assumed Dr Brenner
was dead as the last time we saw him, the

00:08:03.499 --> 00:08:07.039
Demogorgon appeared to be pouncing on him
in the school corridor, though the camera

00:08:07.039 --> 00:08:09.830
cut away before we could confirm his fate.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:14.460
In Season 2, Papa makes an eerie appearance
when Kali uses her powers to summon him up

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.710
in El's mind.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:19.530
But what's really exciting for season 3 and
beyond is that former Hawkins Lab worker,

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:23.759
Ray, tells El and Kali that Brenner is still
alive and that he can lead them to the man

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:25.800
who called himself their father.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.589
Of course, Kali and El are about to wreak
revenge on Ray for what he did to them and

00:08:29.589 --> 00:08:33.340
El's mother at the Lab, so it's possible he's
lying to save his neck.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.880
But if we take Ray's confession at face value,
where is Brenner hiding?

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:40.250
Perhaps in Chicago, like his former Lab assistant.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.950
And what is Brenner doing?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.819
Working on a number Twelve, maybe.

00:08:43.819 --> 00:08:47.069
And will El be able to locate him by herself?

00:08:47.069 --> 00:08:51.259
It'll also be intriguing to find out whether
Brenner is actually Eleven's biological father,

00:08:51.259 --> 00:08:56.150
or whether, more likely, he was just encouraging
her to think of him as 'papa' as a convenient

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:59.410
way for them to bond and get her to do as
he wished.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:03.740
The seventh episode wasn't as well received
as the rest of the show by many fans as it

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.860
felt somewhat jarring in terms of the setting
and characters.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.050
But what Eleven learned from Kali was vital
for the finale.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:14.259
However, whether we'll see Kali return might
well depend on whether the Duffer Brothers

00:09:14.259 --> 00:09:17.770
feel she's important for the final defeat
of the Shadow Monster.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:22.380
She could return as a potential antagonist
to Eleven given they departed on difficult

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:26.060
terms, however, they regard each other as
sisters so it's more likely they'll join together

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.870
next season to find and deal with Dr Brenner.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.589
Now, what do you want to see happen in Season
3 and what are your favourite moments from

00:09:33.589 --> 00:09:34.730
this season?

